[
    {
        "content": "<p>This question is a continuation of my journey to understand various interplays between constructors and type constructor. My previous questions are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/About.20parameters.2C.20indices.2C.20and.20inductive.2EautoPromoteIndices/with/574800302\">About parameters, indices, and inductive.autoPromoteIndices</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/For.20which.20constructors.20.60inj.60.20is.20generated.3F\">For which constructors inj is generated?</a> </li>\n</ul>\n<p>Subsingletons are defined in the language reference as proposition satisfying:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>There is at most one constructor.</li>\n<li>Each of the constructor's parameter types is either a <code>Prop</code>, a parameter, or an index.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let me use terminology based on <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/About.20parameters.2C.20indices.2C.20and.20inductive.2EautoPromoteIndices/with/574800302\">help</a> from <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"306601\">@Kyle Miller</span>: \"The parameters of an inductive type consist of the largest prefix of arguments shared by the type constructor and all the constructors. The remaining arguments of the type constructor are called indices, and the remaining arguments of a constructor are called fields.\"</p>\n<p>The first bullet of the definition of a subsingleton is clear and so is the case of an argument of type <code>Prop</code>. I am tempted to reformulate the second bullet as:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each argument of the constructor has type <code>Prop</code> or has a type occurring in the domain of the type constructor.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It seems that the parameters index distinction is unnecessary since together they cover everything. Is this correct? (Edited since I realized that my previous formulation was clearly incorrect.)</p>",
        "id": 576896321,
        "sender_full_name": "Lauri Oksanen",
        "timestamp": 1772519542
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Let's see what the kernel thinks (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/03a5db34c77db5266d21af56469ba43c9965d341/src/kernel/inductive.cpp#L479-L534\"><code>elim_only_at_universe_zero</code></a>). According to the kernel, the recursor of an inductive can eliminate into any universe iff the inductive type's universe is never zero (i.e. the inductive type is never a proposition) <em>or</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li>The inductive type isn't mutual, <strong>and</strong></li>\n<li>There is at most one constructor, <strong>and</strong></li>\n<li>If there is a constructor, then for any field <code>x : ty</code>:<br>\n    1. <code>ty</code> is a proposition (i.e. <code>x</code> is a proof), <strong>or</strong><br>\n    2. <code>x</code> occurs in the argument list of the result type of the constructor. Since <code>x</code> is not a parameter that means that <code>x</code> must be set as an index in the result type.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>So, the complete correct property for large elimination for propositional inductives is<br>\n\"The inductive type is not mutual, and has at most one constructor where all fields are proofs or indices\"</p>",
        "id": 576975796,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1772544666
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks a lot! Does 3.2 mean that <code>x : ty</code> would have been promoted to a parameter if wasn't preceded by an index in the type constructor or a field in the constructor (assuming <code>inductive.autoPromoteIndices</code>)? It is an argument that is shared by the type constructor and the constructor (hence all the constructors as there is at most one of them), right? (Edited: added \"or a field in the constructor\")</p>",
        "id": 577176148,
        "sender_full_name": "Lauri Oksanen",
        "timestamp": 1772618176
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, using the following script:</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>Script to find cases where 3.2 matters</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getEnv</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">constants</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inductInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continue</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ctor</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ctors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continue</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">forallTelescopeReducing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">whnfType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"what\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">unless</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isAlwaysZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">recInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getConstInfoRec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkRecName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">recInfo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">levelParams</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">levelParams</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctorInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getConstInfoCtor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">forallTelescope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctorInfo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fields</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vars</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">drop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctorInfo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">numParams</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">unless</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fields</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">allM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isProof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>you can find that the only ones where this matters are <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Acc#doc\">docs#Acc</a>, <code>Acc.below</code> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Functor.IsHomLift#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Functor.IsHomLift</a> (for all others 3.1 is enough).<br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Functor.IsHomLift#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Functor.IsHomLift</a> fits your description of having another index before (in that case <code>p.map φ</code>). <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Acc#doc\">docs#Acc</a> is the real important one:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The reason <code>x</code> doesn't become a parameter here is that the value is different in a recursive occurrence (<code>Acc r y</code> instead of <code>Acc r x</code>). Otherwise, this rule ensures that things you <em>could</em> promote to parameters don't prevent large elimination (even without <code>autoPromoteIndices</code>).</p>",
        "id": 577201696,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1772625611
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is very helpful. I need to take one step back since my attempt \"The parameters of an inductive type consist of the largest prefix of arguments shared by the type constructor and all the constructors. The remaining arguments of the type constructor are called indices, and the remaining arguments of a constructor are called fields.\" is incorrect in view of <code>Acc</code>. </p>\n<p>Uniformity of an argument must be defined first and then \"The parameters of an inductive type consist of the largest prefix of <strong>uniform</strong> arguments shared by the type constructor and all the constructors. The remaining arguments of the type constructor are called indices, and the remaining arguments of a constructor are called fields.\" </p>\n<p>Here is an attempt to be very formal. \"Consider the saturated applications of the type constructor <code>T</code> of an inductive type that occur in the definition of the constructors of the type. Let <code>T a1 ... an</code> and <code>T b1 ... bn</code> be any such applications. The j-th argument of <code>T</code> is <em>uniform</em> if <code>aj</code> and <code>bj</code> are definitionally equal.\"</p>",
        "id": 577360180,
        "sender_full_name": "Lauri Oksanen",
        "timestamp": 1772660428
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the elaborator actually checks that the arguments are syntactically equal, not just definitionally but otherwise this sounds right</p>",
        "id": 577362682,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1772661383
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And I guess you could also rephrase the subsingleton criterion as<br>\n\"There is at most one constructor where all arguments are proofs or arguments of the type constructor\"</p>",
        "id": 577363127,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1772661567
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The reason I wrote \"definitionally equal\" is that trying to force the third argument of <code>Acc</code> to be a parameter </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BadAcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BadAcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BadAcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>gives <code>inductiveParamMismatch</code> error that mentions definitional equality: </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mismatched inductive type parameter in<br>\n<code>BadAcc r y</code><br>\nThe provided argument<br>\n<code>α</code><br>\nis not definitionally equal to the expected parameter<br>\n<code>α✝</code></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 577408815,
        "sender_full_name": "Lauri Oksanen",
        "timestamp": 1772683892
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Definitional equality is indeed an incorrect notion, as demonstrated by </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NotAcc3Params</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NotAcc3Params</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">NotAcc3Params</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>vs</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NotAcc2Params</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NotAcc2Params</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">NotAcc2Params</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Trying once again: \"Consider a prefix <code>α1 → … → αj</code> shared by the type constructor <code>T</code> and all constructors <code>c1, …, cm</code> of an inductive type. The prefix is <em>uniform</em> if for each <code>n=1, …, m</code>, writing <code>cn : (a1 : α1) → … → (aj : αj) → xn</code>, every occurrence of <code>T</code> in <code>xn</code> is of the form <code>T a1 … aj …</code>.</p>\n<p>The <em>parameters</em> of an inductive type consist of the largest uniform prefix shared by the type constructor and all the constructors.\"</p>",
